    "result": "I added the two roles, but I could not run the tests. The permission prompt blocked `go test` and I cannot approve it here. Run `go test ./...` to check.\n\n- **The table:** each role now maps to one set of permissions in `perms.go`, and every `CanX` function reads that table. A role that is not in the table, or has the wrong case, gets nothing.\n- **Owner:** has everything admin has, plus `CanTransfer(role string) bool`, which only owner passes.\n- **Auditor:** can read and export, and nothing else.\n- **`sharing.go`:** I rewrote `CanExport` and `CanInvite` to read the same table. Before, `CanExport` let any non-empty unknown role export (`\"guest\"`, `\"Admin\"`). That now returns false, which changes behavior for anyone who relied on it.\n- **New file `perms_test.go`:** tests every role against every check, plus unknown and wrong-case names.\n\n**TLDR**\nAdded auditor and owner roles and `CanTransfer`, all driven by one role table in `perms.go`. Unknown roles can no longer export.\nTests not run: approve `go test ./...`.",
